{"title":"1957 AHSME Problems/Problem 34","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The points that satisfy the system <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b479e4a8dc1d551b765c7d0ac03e1d224cc929.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = 1,\\, x^2 + y^2 &lt; 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"185\" height=\"18\" />, constitute the following set: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04eacedd19dff8f1d1f46a6d466e166d6b0cf10b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{only two points} \\qquad \\\\  \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{an arc of a circle}\\qquad \\\\  \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{a straight line segment not including the end-points}\\qquad\\\\  \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{a straight line segment including the end-points}\\qquad\\\\  \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{a single point}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"410\" height=\"96\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8d0c917ef633c50269b9ae3fab786f05a474f55.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import geometry;  // Axes draw((0,-8)--(0,8),arrow=Arrows); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,9)); draw((-8,0)--(8,0),arrow=Arrows); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(9,0));  // Circle and Line draw(circle((0,0),5),red+dashed); draw(line((0,1),(1,0)),blue);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/476aee07c9af5110b8769e3534ef896fab9368ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> is in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Standard_form\" title=\"Standard form\">standard form</a>. Thus, it has a slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1ec53b9e4fea7e2c8d0c0e2de13c6e2c8f21e425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\tfrac{1}{1}=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"74\" height=\"23\" /> and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-intercept at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. It is graphed in blue in the diagram. All the points that satisfy this system must lie on this line. \n</p><p>The inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/2/d42ab8a83f1e5cd4a1ad328702d789db094fb492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2&lt;25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" /> is true for all points <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Strict_inequality\" title=\"Strict inequality\">strictly</a> less than <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distance_formula\" title=\"Distance formula\">distance</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/5/fb5b3770ccfcced49bb6cebfd0407f280789474f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{25}=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"21\" /> from the origin. This area is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Disk\" title=\"Disk\">disk</a> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, whose open boundary is represented in red in the diagram.\n</p><p>Because the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-intercept of the line, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be11a56a55425d6c6b69f70f5fa98eab95e8ad18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, is inside the disk, it cannot be tangent to the disk. Thus, there must be infiniely many points along the line which are within the disk and thereby satisfy the system. However, because the inequality is strict, the segment of solutions does not include the endpoints, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ffcd7e76757fbc9e44ba3a1b417732a276f75c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{\\textbf{(C)} a straight line segment not including the end-points}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"424\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems/Problem_34&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME\" title=\"1957 AHSME\">1957 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1957 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1957_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1957 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1957\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n